│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces the single-pass least-loaded greedy policy with a            │
│                          │ multi-start minimax construction followed by deterministic local refinement. Inspired by  │
│                          │ the original program’s use of KVPR-aware placement and memory feasibility checks, it      │
│                          │ evaluates the *resulting* GPU pressure for each candidate assignment rather than only the │
│                          │ current pressure.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The novel component is a lexicographic minimax search: several complementary model        │
│                          │ orderings are constructed, the best feasible placement is selected by its sorted KVPR     │
│                          │ profile, and then relocation and swap moves are repeatedly applied whenever they improve  │
│                          │ that profile. This directly prioritizes reducing the maximum KVPR while using             │
│                          │ lower-ranked GPU pressures as tie-breakers, and it always preserves memory constraints.   │
