│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ prospective_kvpr_rebalancing                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current-state greedy choice with a prospective minimax choice: each model is  │
│                          │ assigned to the GPU that produces the lowest maximum KVPR after the model is added,       │
│                          │ rather than the GPU with the lowest KVPR before placement. This directly matches the      │
│                          │ optimization objective and accounts for both the model’s request pressure and its memory  │
│                          │ consumption.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A lightweight relocation refinement then repeatedly moves one already placed model        │
│                          │ whenever that strictly lowers the global maximum KVPR. This corrects greedy decisions     │
│                          │ made early in the placement while preserving memory feasibility at every step. Models are │
│                          │ never overcommitted, and a GPU with no remaining KV-cache memory is treated as having     │
│                          │ infinite pressure.                                                                        │
