│ patch_description        │ The previous approach uses one demand-first greedy ordering, followed by strictly         │
│                          │ max-KVPR-improving moves and swaps. Its key parameters are the model ordering `(req_rate  │
│                          │ / slo, model_size)`, one greedy construction pass, an improvement bound of `len(models) * │
│                          │ gpu_num`, and an improvement threshold of `1e-12`.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version improves placement quality with a deterministic multi-start configuration.   │
│                          │ It constructs several initial placements using different selection criteria: high request │
│                          │ pressure first, large-memory models first, pressure-per-memory first, and mixed           │
│                          │ pressure/size orderings. Each greedy decision minimizes the full sorted GPU-pressure      │
│                          │ vector, not only the current maximum, which also balances secondary bottleneck GPUs. The  │
│                          │ best initial placement is then improved with bottleneck-focused moves and swaps. Local    │
│                          │ search accepts lexicographic pressure-vector improvements, allowing equal-maximum moves   │
│                          │ that reduce secondary pressure and create better future improvements. The search uses an  │
│                          │ adaptive iteration budget proportional to both model and GPU count.                       │
