│ patch_name               │ multistart_kvpr_repair                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses one pressure-first ordering and up to `len(models)`             │
│                          │ bottleneck-only move/swap repairs. Its key limitations are construction-order sensitivity │
│                          │ and fragmentation from placing large models too late.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version uses five deterministic construction orders: pressure-first, size-first,     │
│                          │ pressure-density-first, hard-to-place-first (`size / 80` plus density), and a             │
│                          │ large-model-priority ordering. Each start selects the GPU minimizing the resulting global │
│                          │ maximum KVPR, then performs strict-improvement move and swap repair across all GPUs. The  │
│                          │ best feasible placement from all starts is returned. The repair iteration limit is        │
│                          │ increased to `2 * len(models)`, while accepting only improvements larger than `1e-12`,    │
│                          │ ensuring termination.                                                                     │
