│ patch_name               │ postfit_exchange_refinement                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Evaluate GPUs by their KVPR after placing a model rather than by their current KVPR,      │
│                          │ preventing greedy assignments from overlooking the pressure induced by the new model.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Then add a bounded local-search refinement phase. It accepts only strict lexicographic    │
│                          │ improvements to the complete sorted GPU-pressure vector, so it minimizes the maximum KVPR │
│                          │ first and improves secondary bottlenecks without regressing worse GPUs. The neighborhood  │
│                          │ includes moves, swaps, one-for-two exchanges, and the reverse pair-for-one exchanges. The │
│                          │ reverse exchange is important for memory-constrained placements: two smaller bottleneck   │
│                          │ models can be consolidated onto another GPU while a larger model is moved back, enabling  │
│                          │ improvements unreachable by one-for-two exchanges alone. Every candidate explicitly       │
│                          │ validates post-exchange GPU memory.                                                       │
