│ patch_description        │ Extend local refinement with reverse two-for-one exchanges. A single relocation cannot    │
│                          │ improve placements where a bottleneck GPU must give up two smaller models in exchange for │
│                          │ one larger model from another GPU to rebalance both memory and request pressure. The new  │
│                          │ neighborhood examines pairs only on current bottleneck GPUs, verifies both resulting      │
│                          │ memory capacities, and accepts only a strict lexicographic improvement of the sorted KVPR │
│                          │ profile. This guarantees that the maximum KVPR never increases while allowing             │
│                          │ improvements that are unreachable through single-model moves.                             │
