│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ fix_moves_add_unlock                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The relocation loop currently records an improved profile but never records the           │
│                          │ corresponding move, so direct improving moves are never applied. Fixing this enables the  │
│                          │ existing local-search phase to reach substantially better placements.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, add a bounded deterministic two-step unlock search after swaps fail. It     │
│                          │ temporarily evacuates a small candidate model from a target GPU to create capacity, then  │
│                          │ moves a high-pressure model off one of the two most pressured GPUs into that target. Both │
│                          │ intermediate and final placements remain memory-feasible; the intermediate pressure is    │
│                          │ bounded, and the final placement is accepted only when it strictly improves the KVPR      │
│                          │ profile. This repairs capacity-blocked hotspots without introducing broad expensive       │
│                          │ search.                                                                                   │
