│ patch_name               │ three_gpu_relocation_chain                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Add a capacity-safe two-model relocation chain when neither a direct relocation nor a     │
│                          │ swap improves the placement. A common local optimum occurs when a high-pressure GPU needs │
│                          │ to move a model to a nearly full target GPU, but that target must first send one of its   │
│                          │ models to a third GPU. This three-GPU operation changes the assignment more flexibly than │
│                          │ a swap while retaining the strict lexicographic KVPR improvement requirement, so the      │
│                          │ maximum KVPR never increases. The search is bounded for large workloads to preserve the   │
│                          │ current lightweight runtime behavior.                                                     │
