│ patch_description        │ Add a two-for-one exchange neighborhood before the three-GPU chain search. A KVPR         │
│                          │ bottleneck can be caused by several high-demand small models sharing a GPU; relocating or │
│                          │ swapping just one of them may not improve the maximum pressure. Exchanging two such       │
│                          │ models for one lower-pressure model can simultaneously rebalance demand and residual      │
│                          │ memory. The neighborhood is restricted to current bottleneck GPUs and small instances,    │
│                          │ preserving the existing fast execution behavior.                                          │
