│ patch_name               │ residual_aware_orders                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Add two deterministic model-arrival orders that explicitly account for residual-memory    │
│                          │ fragmentation. Large models become disproportionately difficult to place once any GPU has │
│                          │ been partially filled, especially models whose size consumes a large fraction of the 80   │
│                          │ GB GPU. The new orders prioritize this risk using size relative to residual capacity and  │
│                          │ a large-item-first key.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The existing candidate GPU selection and threshold feasibility logic remain unchanged, so │
│                          │ every selected assignment still obeys both physical memory and transformed KVPR capacity. │
│                          │ These additional starts only broaden the packing constructions considered at each         │
│                          │ threshold, improving the chance of finding a feasible packing at a lower maximum KVPR     │
│                          │ threshold.                                                                                │
