│ patch_description        │ Add a threshold-feasibility construction based on the KVPR inequality. For a target       │
│                          │ pressure `p`, a GPU is valid exactly when its assigned models satisfy `sum(weight + p *   │
│                          │ model_size) <= p * GPU_MEM_SIZE`. This transforms the nonlinear pressure constraint into  │
│                          │ a bin-capacity constraint.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new construction binary-searches for a low feasible pressure threshold and packs      │
│                          │ transformed model sizes with several deterministic orders. Candidate GPU selection uses   │
│                          │ the requested stronger tie-break: projected maximum pressure, projected second-highest    │
│                          │ pressure, transformed remaining capacity, and physical remaining memory. The previous     │
│                          │ greedy and local-search candidates remain available, so this only adds stronger           │
│                          │ placements rather than replacing existing successful behavior.                            │
