│ patch_description        │ Add a construction order derived from the KVPR feasibility transformation. For a          │
│                          │ candidate maximum pressure T, each GPU must satisfy `load + T * model_memory <= T *       │
│                          │ GPU_MEM_SIZE`; therefore a model’s effective packing weight is `demand + T * size`. Using │
│                          │ the global lower bound on T as the estimate prioritizes models that are difficult in both │
│                          │ request pressure and memory, reducing fragmentation that can prevent the greedy and       │
│                          │ local-search phases from reaching a lower bottleneck. This is an additional deterministic │
│                          │ start, so existing successful starts and feasibility fallback remain unchanged.           │
